      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Aragon sits on the former Old Fort Tularosa site, built in 1872 to guard the Apache Agency and its Warm Springs residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aragon%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1937 parish became a cultural hub, and its parochial school opened in 1951, closing in the early 1970s as enrollment fell.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/aragon_new_mexico",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Aragon sits at about 7,135 feet elevation, on high desert plateaus that narrow into the Tularosa River valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
